27. Rc8+ { I assume you have calculated this check before capturing the queen! } Qf8! { Good calculation! This move must have been seen before capturing the queen on e3. } 
28. Rxf8+ Kxf8 $19  { Black emerges with an extra rook and a winning position. This example once again shows the importance of short and accurate calculations.

In this course, you'll face such short calculations designed to overcome resistance and justify moves that initially appear to be blunders. These puzzles are crafted to be both engaging and thought-provoking, teaching you to look beyond the surface and avoid dismissing moves simply because they seem like mistakes at first glance. } 
