What did we learn from this example?

Once again, this example demonstrates the importance of combining 'C' (Checks) and 'L' (Loose Pieces or Squares) in our checklist. The move 17...Nxe5⁇ allowed a devastating check on d8, which was White's only check in that position. Moreover, moving the knight to e5 unprotected a key square: d8.

