This example also highlights the danger of tunnel vision. While playing 11. Nc3⁇, White was solely focused on the weak e4-pawn and failed to consider that the bishop on b4 would run out of squares after Nc3, leading to its capture. } ( 12.Bc5 $4 { Blundering into the trap: } 12...b6! { The bishop on c5 got trapped, as it had no safe escape squares against this attack by the black pawn. } ) *

