{ While the Rule of the Square is a useful guideline, it cannot be followed blindly, as there are key exceptions every chess player should know. One such exception is this classic breakthrough tactic, where the opponent can force one of our own pawns or pieces to block our king’s path, preventing it from entering the square of the passed pawn. } 48... Kxg5 $4  { The Black king captures the wrong pawn (we'll analyze the correct move in the next puzzle). At first glance, it seems that White cannot create an unstoppable passed pawn, as the Black king is well within reach of the e5 and f5 pawns. However, everything changes after a precise move sequence: } 
