50. e6! {[%cal Ge6e8,Ge6g8,Gg8g6,Gg6e6,Rg5f6,Gh5g6,Rg5g6][%csl Rg5,Rf6,Rg6]} { The point of the previous move, and an important pattern to know in pawn endgames. The black king cannot enter the square of the e6-pawn due to the f6-pawn blocking its access on that square, while the pawn on h5 is preventing ...Kg6. The e6-pawn becomes unstoppable and White wins after } f5 
51. e7 $18  { This was an important pawn endgame chunk that helps make you more vigilant on potential breakthrough ideas by your opponents, while making it easier to find them yourself and win games. } *

