It's important to observe how the black king and rook ended up on the same color square as the enemy knight on g6, enabling the fork. However, it’s crucial not to overgeneralize this rule: the strongest move, 20...Rh7!, also places the rook and king on the same color as the enemy knight, yet it doesn't allow a check or fork.

Additionally, this example highlights the importance of recognizing potentially 'trappable' pieces, such as the knight on g6 (Mobility restrictions). The knight on g6 became stranded deep in the enemy camp, and Black skillfully punished it by carefully maneuvering to avoid any forks, ultimately sealing the knight's fate.

