{ The black rook just hit the white queen on c2. What should White play? } 24. Rb2 {[%mdl 32768]} {[%csl Re2,Rc2]} { One of the two good ways to parry the threat. White offers a rook trade and achieves an equal position. } ( 24.Qd1 $10 { This was also a good move, carefully retreating the queen and keeping the e2-knight guarded against the attack by the rook on a2. } ) ( 24.Qb3 $4 { This would be a blunder as it leaves the e2-knight undefended against the attack by the rook on a2. } 24...Qxb3 25.Rxb3 Rxe2 $19 { Black wins the piece and achieves a winning ending.

Here White blundered as they interpreted 23...Ra2 only as a one-sided move (it was only the queen that was targeted). White did not notice the loose knight on e2, which would be directly exposed to the rook on a2 once the queen moves. Right after ...Ra2 was played, the white queen got tied down in guarding that knight on e2, and moving the queen to b3 turned that loose knight into a hanging piece. } ) Rxb2 
